===Numeral===
{{head|en|numeral}}

# {{cln|en|cardinal numbers}} A [[numerical]] [[value]] after [[two]] and before [[four]]. Represented in Arabic digits as [[3]]; this many dots (•••).
#* {{RQ:Grey Riders|8|passage=Venters began to count them—one—two—'''three'''—four—on up to sixteen.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1995|author=Nancy Berliner; Sarah Handler|title=Friends of the House|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=3P0MAAAAYAAJ|isbn=0883891344|page=79
|passage=There is a soft-mat seat (which originally had a palm fiber underwebbing) supported by '''three''' curved transverse braces.}}
#* {{quote-av|en|actor={{w|Jennifer Hale}} as Samantha “Sam” and {{w|Andrea Baker|Andrea Taylor}}|title=w:Totally Spies!|season=2|number=1|text=Okay, '''on three''', we open the door and jump on the rope. One, two…<br>Wait, wait! Do we go on three? Or do we go on “go”?<br>Three! Who said anything about “go”?|role=Clover|episode=A Spy is Born Part II|writers=Michelle Lamoreaux; Robert Lamoreaux|network=w:Teletoon|publisher=w:Marathon Media|date=Apr 7 2003}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title={{w|Batman: Arkham City}}|text=Why should she care? One…two…<br>Do we shoot '''on three'''?<br>Yes '''on three'''. Like one, two, '''three''', shoot.|role=Joker thugs|writers=w:Paul Dini; Paul Crocker; w:Sefton Hill|network=w:Rocksteady Studios|publisher=w:Warner Bros. Interactive Entertainment|date=2011-10-18}}
